{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E89EC0BE36E642B4CF9B1208D8AFD807/jobs/348479": {
      "title": "Associate  Director Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Associate  Director Alumni Engagement You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Associate  Director Alumni Engagement Oglethorpe University - Atlanta, GA 30319 Apply Overview Position Type Full-Time Staff Job Shift Day Education Level Bachelor's Category Education Apply Description Oglethorpe University is seeking an Associate Director for the Office of Alumni Engagement. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President of Advancement, this individual is responsible for helping develop and strengthen a pipeline of engaged alumni through the entire lifecycle, ultimately resulting in increased participation and giving. The Assistant Director is responsible for the successful planning, execution, and post-evaluation of alumni events, volunteer opportunities, and other special initiatives, while building and strengthening relationships with alumni to increase engagement. They will also serve as the staff advisor to the Student Alumni Association, a student organization that works to bridge the gap between students and alumni. The role includes direct supervision of one part-time student worker. Responsibilities: EVENTS Lead all aspects of campus and regional alumni engagement events, including location decisions, logistics, volunteer management, and budget oversight. Solicit feedback for program enhancements and integrate into engagement and leadership cultivation strategies. In support of events and programming, identify, cultivate, and strengthen relationships with alumni in addition to maximizing existing relationships in collaboration with other Advancement Team members. VOLUNTEER MANAGEMENT AND DEVELOPMENT Serve as the primary staff liaison to the Alumni Board, managing board operations, coordinating meetings and committee activities, supporting member engagement, and advancing strategic initiatives aligned with the university’s mission. Collaborate with campus partners to identify alumni volunteer opportunities. Identify, cultivate, and recruit alumni volunteer leadership through personal visits, email, and phone contacts. Meet with alumni and build participation in all areas of the University. Support the logistics of events, meetings, activities, panels, mixers, etc. to result in successful volunteer experiences, continued engagement, and a sustainable leadership pipeline. Manage the Student Alumni Association by planning and facilitating a program of student engagement opportunities that provide them with a unique link to the alumni association. Recruit students to join the Student Alumni Association. Recruit student volunteers through the Student Alumni Association for event assistance as needed throughout the year. COMMUNICATIONS Manage the alumni social media and webpages. Work with the Marketing department to create digital marketing content for the alumni website and social media pages. Provide content for the alumni newsletter, which is designed and created by the Marketing department. Create marketing material for events as needed. Supervise a student worker to assist with graphic needs. Work with the Marketing department to provide a vision for printed mail pieces, including but not limited to Alumni Weekend mailer, Hall of Fame program, and alumni events postcard. CAMPUS RELATIONS Collaborate with colleagues across university divisions and departments to explore partnership opportunities for alumni volunteers and share information. Build relationships around campus to create a cohesive picture of alumni engagement at Oglethorpe. Attend campus and partner events to further the relationship and increase visibility on campus. DATABASE MANAGEMENT Work with Development Operations to ensure accurate and complete alumni database records in Raiser’s Edge Blackbaud. Input contact reports and volunteer instances in the database in a timely manner. Create event pages, send marketing emails, and pull basic queries in Raiser’s Edge Blackbaud. Qualifications Requirements: Bachelor's degree and a minimum of 2-4 years of experience in event planning, alumni relations/ development and/or related field. Strong organizational and communication skills. Ability to facilitate collaborative relationships and work in a team environment. Desire to mentor students. Availability to work occasional nights and weekends, along with overnight travel. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds. Share job details to About OGLETHORPE UNIVERSITY INC Oglethorpe University Turner Lynch Campus Center Stormy Petrel Academic Quad Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E89EC0BE36E642B4CF9B1208D8AFD807/jobs/347055": {
      "title": "Director Advancement Operations",
      "description": "Director Advancement Operations You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director Advancement Operations Oglethorpe University - Atlanta, GA 30319 Apply Overview Position Type Full-Time Staff Education Level Bachelor's Category Education Apply Description Reporting to the Senior Director of Advancement Operations, the Director of Advancement serves as a bridge between key functions in Oglethorpe University’s Advancement system. The position bridges advancement operations, data management and services, and annual donor engagement and fundraising activities to positively contribute to the overall success of the University Advancement team. PRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES The Director of Advancement is responsible for the following key functions: 1. Gift Processing & Reconciliation Ensures that daily gift processing and gift acknowledgement processes are completed in a timely and accurate fashion Performs gift processing and gift review as needed Supports the Advancement Operations Manager in monthly gift reconciliation processes 2. Data Management & Services Uses the Raiser’s Edge database to create queries, exports, dashboards, and reports Uses Raiser’s Edge to fulfill complex data requests from Advancement colleagues Produces weekly and on-demand financial fundraising reports for Advancement stakeholders Provides data set-up and support for Advancement events and fundraising appeals Manages and supports the completion of annual and periodic data clean-up projects Manages and supports the completion of annual and periodic data imports and updates Collaborates cross-functionally with campus partners to facilitate data sharing, ensure data integrity, and reconcile records across institutional systems 3. Data Analysis and Prospect Management Uses Raiser’s Edge tools and features to conduct donor analysis, comparative giving analysis, fundraising performance analysis, and more for the purpose of generating actionable insights Uses Raiser’s Edge Prospect Insight tools to identify strong prospects, build prospect lists, and improve the portfolios of frontline fundraisers Other Expectations Uses technology to track and manage projects and tasks Consistently meets project and task deadlines Provides task support to Operations and other Advancement colleagues as needed Provides event support for Advancement events (including weekend and evening events) Actively participates in Advancement and institutional staff meetings, trainings, and convenings Performs other related duties as assigned to support the needs and objectives of Advancement Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS The Director of Advancement must meet the three qualifications below to be considered for the position: Proficiency using Raiser’s Edge (or a similar donor CRM) Proficiency with Microsoft Excel and Word A minimum of 5 years of Advancement experience with proven success *Applicants without Raiser’s Edge or similar donor CRM experience should not apply. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS A strong candidate for the Director of Development position will have the following qualifications: A bachelor’s degree or higher from a nationally accredited university Proficiency using project management tools, preferably Asana and Microsoft Teams Analytical thinking skills; strong organizational skills; efficient task management; and excellent customer service and interpersonal skills Collaborative and supportive team mindset BENEFITS Affordable health, dental, and vision insurance Employer-matched retirement plan Generous paid time off (PTO), including vacation, sick leave, and paid holidays Hybrid work opportunities Share job details to About OGLETHORPE UNIVERSITY INC Oglethorpe University Turner Lynch Campus Center Stormy Petrel Academic Quad Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E89EC0BE36E642B4CF9B1208D8AFD807/jobs/342318": {
      "title": "Reference & Instruction Librarian",
      "description": "Reference & Instruction Librarian You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Reference & Instruction Librarian Oglethorpe University - Atlanta, GA 30319 Apply Overview Position Type Full-Time Faculty Education Level Master's Category Education Apply Description Summary/Function: The Oglethorpe University Library seeks a Research and Instruction Librarian who will provide forward-thinking and learner-centered information literacy research and instructional services to the Oglethorpe campus community.  This librarian will play a vital role in coordinating instructional services and in furthering the research and teaching mission of Oglethorpe University. This role will be responsible for developing a robust instruction and outreach program, both in-person and online, for providing research consultations to both students and faculty, and for crafting online learning resources for the campus community. The Research and Instruction Librarian will develop classes and workshops that address a changing information and technological environment and will create learning materials and experiences to reach student and faculty audiences at their point of need. This position promotes collaboration, develops dynamic learning experiences for students, and assists with development and implementation of assessment initiatives aimed at improving services and collections. This role also collaborates with a broad range of stakeholders to conceptualize, define, and deliver dynamic instruction and research consultation services. The Research and Instruction Librarian may also provide outreach to non-academic units, develop events and services that promote the library, and perform other duties/functions as assigned. Duties and Responsibilities: Coordinate, plan, and implement instruction services, in-person and online, including information literacy workshops, class-based instruction, and asynchronous online learning materials. Teach research instruction sessions for subjects and academic programs across campus, working strategically with the faculty and instructors to integrate information literacy into courses. Create and maintain online instructional resources and guides for the Oglethorpe campus community. Provide reference assistance to members of the Oglethorpe community in a variety of formats, including research consultations and reference chat services Evaluate and assess the library’s instructional services and programs. Collaborate with faculty to develop, design, execute, and assess research assignments and projects to enhance student’s information literacy skills and knowledge. Provide outreach services and events for the Oglethorpe campus community, including orientation sessions for faculty and students. Offer orientations o library services to faculty and students Promote library services and resources to the Oglethorpe community Coordinates the selection, licensing, and delivery of electronic resources Assists in maintaining electronic resources and the library website by updating links, troubleshooting, and providing user support as needed. Serve on staff and faculty committees Assist with library outreach, programming, and social media Commit to ongoing professional development, scholarly contribution, and service to the University and library profession. All other duties as assigned by the Director of the Library. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Masters degree in library and information science from an ALA-accredited program, or a related field Experience providing library instruction services in an academic library setting Experience providing reference services, including consultations and/or chat services, to an undergraduate student population Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in a team-oriented academic environment. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal skills Preferred Qualifications Experience in planning information literacy education and research help services, with demonstrated knowledge of best practices. Experience in creating and maintaining online learning resources Experience in providing outreach services in an academic library setting Prior experience in an academic library setting Application materials must include a Cover letter and Curriculum Vita (CV) or Resume. We are extending the application deadline to allow for additional qualified applicants. Please apply by October 8 for best consideration. The position will remain open until filled.” Work Environment/Physical Demands: The position is in a normal office environment; an alternative work schedule may be required; typically requires sitting at a desk or table and repetitive wrist, hand or finger movement; occasional lifting up to 20 lbs; use of office equipment will also be required. About Oglethorpe University Founded in 1835, Oglethorpe University is a liberal arts college that unites a close-knit campus community with the big city culture and opportunities of Atlanta, Georgia. Today, the university enrolls over 1,400 students, representing 33 states and 31 countries, and offers students Atlanta’s premiere undergraduate learning experience. Students at Oglethorpe benefit from small classes and close connections to our outstanding faculty. Oglethorpe University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer committed to inclusive excellence. Oglethorpe prohibits discrimination against all applicants and employees based on race; age; color; religion; national origin or ancestry; sex; sexual orientation; gender; gender identity or gender expression; marital status; pregnancy; childbirth or related medical conditions; disability; genetic information; citizenship status; veteran status; or any other category protected by federal, state or local law. This job description is intended as a summary of the primary responsibilities of and qualifications for this position. The job description is not intended as inclusive of all duties an individual in this position might be asked to perform or of all qualifications that may be required either now or in the future. Share job details to About OGLETHORPE UNIVERSITY INC Oglethorpe University Turner Lynch Campus Center Stormy Petrel Academic Quad Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E89EC0BE36E642B4CF9B1208D8AFD807/jobs/334429": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor Core 103: Music & Culture",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor Core 103: Music & Culture You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor Core 103: Music & Culture Oglethorpe University - Atlanta, GA 30319 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Education Level Master's Travel Percentage None Category Education Apply Description The Oglethorpe University Core Program is seeking adjunct instructors to teach Oglethorpe’s unique Core 103: Music and Culture class during the Fall 2026 semester. Our Core Music and Culture course is an exciting approach to the general education breadth requirement in the arts. Students in this course develop an understanding of the creative process as a means of self-expression and the artist’s relationship to the world. This course examines the styles, trends, and developments of Western and international music from early civilizations through the 20th century. Study and discussion develop an understanding of how music and the cultural arts reflect and affect societal trends and values. Successful applicants must be interested in student-centered teaching. Applicants will be expected to foster an inclusive learning environment by engaging in and promoting diverse teaching, learning, and mentoring communities. Teaching assignments will be based on instructor experience, areas of expertise, and availability. Course sections meet 3 hours/week (either three 60-minute sessions or two 90-minute sessions).  For more information about the teaching schedule, please reach out to the Director of Core Studies, at coredirectors@oglethorpe.edu . Oglethorpe is committed to fostering a campus community and intellectual environment that recruits and maintains diverse faculty and staff, promotes a culture of respect for diverse experiences and perspectives, and understands and addresses the role of inequality in shaping our individual and collective identities. We value faculty mentorship and support faculty teaching, research, and development. Adjunct faculty will be mentored and supported by full-time Art/Core faculty who are committed to excellence in teaching and fostering a collaborative community. The university currently enrolls a diverse population of approximately 1,500 students who represent more than 30 states and 30 countries. More than half of Oglethorpe’s students identify as persons of color and 40 percent are the first in their families to attend college. Candidates from historically excluded groups, whose work furthers the institution’s diversity, equity, and inclusion goals, and who bring varied life experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds are especially encouraged to apply. Qualifications M.A. or M.F.A. in Art or Art History or related field. Compensation: Compensation will be determined based on the number of credit hours taught. $3300/lecture course (4 credit hours) Starting and Ending Dates: New Faculty Orientation and Faculty Retreat are the week of August 17. The semester runs from August 24 to December 4, with final exams in the following week. Final grades for the semester are due on Tuesday, December 15. To Apply : Applicants are asked to submit a brief letter of interest that makes reference to qualifications, commitment to excellence in teaching, and a record of steady contributions to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. In addition, please submit a C.V. (including contact information), and the name and contact information of two references (no letter necessary at this point) as soon as possible .  Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Share job details to About OGLETHORPE UNIVERSITY INC Oglethorpe University Turner Lynch Campus Center Stormy Petrel Academic Quad Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E89EC0BE36E642B4CF9B1208D8AFD807/jobs/333566": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician (Live-in Position)",
      "description": "Maintenance Technician (Live-in Position) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Maintenance Technician (Live-in Position) Oglethorpe University - Atlanta, GA 30319 Apply Overview Position Type Full-Time Staff Education Level High School Diploma Required Category Facilities Apply Description Under the direction of the Maintenance Supervisor, the Facilities Maintenance Technician will be responsible for the University building systems, appliances and infrastructure, including inspecting, testing, repairing, installing, and modifying components in and around buildings. The Facilities Maintenance Technician will prioritize safety and communication in their work and have a working knowledge of all electrical safety regulations.  The Facilities Maintenance Technician will be required to perform various repair tasks and have a strong working knowledge in multiple trades, with demonstrated expertise in carpentry, HVAC, and plumbing. Ability to troubleshoot, prioritize work orders, and maintain building systems with minimal supervision is essential. This is a live-on-campus position working from 2-10:30 pm. The selected candidate is required to reside in employer provided housing located on campus as a condition of employment. Housing and applicable utilities will be provided in accordance to institutional policies. Because of the residential nature of the role, the employee is required to respond to emergencies, critical incidents, or operational needs outside of normal business hours. Duties and Responsibilities: Ability to work independently with minimal supervision to accomplish work efficiently. Ability to analyze problems and make repairs. Working knowledge of carpentry, general repairs, plumbing, and electrical systems in a commercial building setting. Working knowledge of locks and keys is a plus. Repair and paint drywall, and flooring in residence halls. Working knowledge of computer or mobile applications. Use personal protective equipment as required. Ensure proper maintenance and safeguarding of materials and tools against theft or vandalism. Complete required documentation of repairs and service information through the campus work order system. Communicate with management any hazards or risks that require immediate attention. Ensure adequate inventory of necessary supplies and parts Calibrate equipment to provided specifications Drives utility vehicles to and from work sites. Participate in the on-call rotation and respond to calls after hours. Ability to communicate effectively with both internal and external constituents in a collaborative environment Ability to schedule and manage outside vendors when necessary. Prepare and maintain reports and updates to management. Complete additional duties as assigned. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: A high school diploma or equivalent. Minimum 5 years of general maintenance experience.  Experience in a University setting preferred.  Must possess strong knowledge of building trades and preventative maintenance experience; must have strong skills in organization and communication and possess great customer service. Valid Georgia driver’s license and insurable driving record is required. Other Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: The Facilities Maintenance Technician must have basic knowledge of general maintenance; knowledge and experience in building systems, appliances, carpentry and low voltage systems; experience or background in construction is a plus.  Must have good interpersonal skills and be able to work well with supervisors, coworkers, University community and the public. Work Environment/Physical Demands: Majority of the tasks associated with this position will be performed indoors at multiple campus locations or buildings.  Some duties will require the ability to function with exposure to seasonal weather conditions.  May have exposure to potential hazards.  Ability to stand, bend stop, kneel, reach lift pull, push, and walk for a minimum of three hours. Also, must possess the ability to lift at least 45 lbs. using safe lifting techniques. This job description is intended as a summary of the primary responsibilities of and qualifications for this position. The job description is not intended as inclusive of all duties an individual in this position might be asked to perform or of all qualifications that may be required either now or in the future. Share job details to About OGLETHORPE UNIVERSITY INC Oglethorpe University Turner Lynch Campus Center Stormy Petrel Academic Quad Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E89EC0BE36E642B4CF9B1208D8AFD807/jobs/286802": {
      "title": "PT Facilities Support Technician",
      "description": "PT Facilities Support Technician You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account PT Facilities Support Technician Oglethorpe University - Atlanta, GA 30319 Apply Overview Position Type Part-Time Staff Education Level High School Diploma Required Category Entry Level Apply Description Under the direction of the Maintenance Supervisor, the PT Facilities Support Technician (FST) will support the campus through the collecting, loading, and transporting of waste and recycling materials from external collection locations across campus. The PT FST will prioritize safety and communication in their work and have a working knowledge of all safety regulations. Possess a proven ability to read, interpret, and work from diagrams and other documents. The PT FST will support University events set-ups, manage office furniture, perform general maintenance duties as well as perform commercial painting and refinishing of structures, furnishings, and surfaces when needed.  This is a part-time position working approximately 10 to 20 hours per week. Duties and Responsibilities: Responsible for collecting, loading, and transporting waste and recycling materials to include office furniture, laboratory equipment. Lifts and moves equipment that may weigh over 100 pounds Ensures the proper safeguarding of tools and moving equipment. Assists in facility and vehicle management maintenance. May operate trucks and university vehicles. Communicate with the supervisor to ensure work orders are processed on time and labor is completed. Supports the needs of the department by being a team player and having flexibility with work orders and schedule adjustments. Assure that deficiencies are reported via the CMMS system. Communicate with management any hazards or risks that require immediate attention. Takes necessary precautions and uses personal protective equipment as required in keeping with OSHA standards and other applicable regulations when working with hazardous chemicals/waste. May paint, hang and finish drywall. Preps surfaces before beginning a project. Ensure adequate inventory of necessary supplies and parts. Complete additional duties as assigned. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent is required.  The position also requires a valid Georgia driver's license and a satisfactory Motor Vehicle Report (MVR). Experience in a University setting is preferred. Other Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Must possess strong skills in organization, communication, and great customer service. Work Environment/Physical Demands: The majority of the tasks associated with this position will be performed outdoors at multiple campus locations or buildings. Some duties will require the ability to function with exposure to seasonal weather conditions. May have exposure to potential hazards. Ability to stand, bend, stoop, kneel, reach, lift, pull, push, and walk for a minimum of four hours. Also, must possess the ability to lift at least 100 lbs. using safe lifting techniques. This job description is intended as a summary of the primary responsibilities of and qualifications for this position. The job description is not intended as inclusive of all duties an individual in this position might be asked to perform or of all qualifications that may be required either now or in the future. Share job details to About OGLETHORPE UNIVERSITY INC Oglethorpe University Turner Lynch Campus Center Stormy Petrel Academic Quad Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E89EC0BE36E642B4CF9B1208D8AFD807/jobs/277593": {
      "title": "Temporary Housekeeper",
      "description": "Temporary Housekeeper You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Temporary Housekeeper Oglethorpe University - Atlanta, GA 30319 Apply Overview Position Type Seasonal Job Shift All Shifts Available Education Level High School Diploma Required Travel Percentage None Category General Labor Apply Description Under the direction of the Housekeeping Supervisor, this position will be responsible for creating clean, orderly, and attractive facilities in all our campus spaces. Spaces for daily or routine cleaning could include academic buildings, classroom settings, public/common spaces, offices and residence halls.   This is a temporary position expected to last approximately eight weeks. Duties and Responsibilities: Performs cleaning duties in all areas that are assigned. Cleans floors with vacuums, dust mops and/or wet mops Collects and removes trash and recyclable materials and deposits to designated areas Cleans, polishes furniture/fixtures in assigned areas and arranges furniture and/or equipment as directed Operates light power cleaning equipment and performs preventatives maintenance Maintains adequate stock of supplies in bathrooms and storage areas Complete additional duties as assigned. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma or GED with proven housekeeping or hospitability expertise. Must have a working knowledge of trends and methods used for cleaning facilities. Minimum 2 years of housekeeping experience. Great people skills and ability to set and change priorities. Other Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: This position is must have great attention for detail and pride in what they do. must have good interpersonal skills and be able to work well with supervisors, coworkers, University community and the public. Work Environment/Physical Demands: Normal interior building environment; typically standing and walking, hand or finger movement; occasionally lifting 25 lbs. or less; requires use of normal cleaning equipment. This job description is intended as a summary of the primary responsibilities of and qualifications for this position. The job description is not intended as inclusive of all duties an individual in this position might be asked to perform or of all qualifications that may be required either now or in the future. Share job details to About OGLETHORPE UNIVERSITY INC Oglethorpe University Turner Lynch Campus Center Stormy Petrel Academic Quad Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E89EC0BE36E642B4CF9B1208D8AFD807/jobs/145366": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Support Coordinator",
      "description": "Campus Safety Support Coordinator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Campus Safety Support Coordinator Oglethorpe University - Atlanta, GA 30319 Apply Overview Position Type Full-Time Staff Job Shift All Shifts Available Education Level High School Diploma Required Travel Percentage None Category Entry Level Apply Description The Campus Safety Support [RM1] Coordinator provides assistance to students, staff, faculty, and visitors in order to ensure a safe and supportive campus environment. The Campus Safety Support Coordinator acts as a friendly and approachable resource for students, faculty, staff, and visitors fostering a sense of safety and belonging on campus. Assigned shifts are regular but may be subject to change temporarily depending on operational needs. Key Responsibilities: Responds in a supportive, helpful, and calming way to calls for immediate assistance with safety issues, health emergencies maintenance issues, fire alarms, and safety issues. Notifies and interfaces with appropriate campus departments and/or off-campus emergency services to address urgent issues or emergencies in order to ensure a safe resolution. Assists with building and campus control access, including opening and closing of facilities and the gates, lockouts, and other related concerns. Assesses after-hours student concerns and activates the professional staff call-back system as needed. Assists in the administration of the campus parking program, including permit issues, parking-related concerns, and the resolution of parking-related disputes. Assists in the issuance and management of Petrel passes. Circulates through the campus on regular schedules to ensure appropriate building access control, identify any parking concerns, report visible safety issues, and create a visible and helpful presence on campus. Offer directions and information about campus resources and services. Maintain a visible and approachable presence on campus to promote a safe and supportive environment. Document and report incidents or concerns to the appropriate campus authorities. Including grounds or maintenance issues, concerning behavior, or potential safety concerns. Provides accurate and timely documentation through the Campus Safety reporting system [RM1] I believe that the word officer will always connote law enforcement in the context of safety.  Coordinator is a typical entry level title in Student Affairs. Qualifications Qualifications: Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to remain calm and composed in various situations. Strong problem-solving skills and resourcefulness. A friendly and approachable demeanor. Knowledge of campus layout and resources is preferred. Prior experience in a customer service or support role is a plus. High school diploma or equivalent required; additional education or training in a related field is a plus. Working Conditions: Must be able to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends, as needed. This position may require walking and standing for extended periods. The Campus Support Coordinator will primarily work outdoors and may be exposed to various weather conditions. Advancement Opportunities Shift Supervisor positions are available to Support Coordinators demonstrating a high level of proficiency. Benefits for Full-Time Staff In addition to a competitive hourly wage, Oglethorpe University offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes life insurance in the amount of your annual salary, LTD insurance, tuition remission for you and your dependents, 403(b) retirement savings plan with employer match as well as health, dental and vision insurance. In addition, all full-time employees receive a generous paid time off policy. Share job details to About OGLETHORPE UNIVERSITY INC Oglethorpe University Turner Lynch Campus Center Stormy Petrel Academic Quad Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E89EC0BE36E642B4CF9B1208D8AFD807/jobs/351165": {
      "title": "PT University Events A/V Support Staff",
      "description": "PT University Events A/V Support Staff You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account PT University Events A/V Support Staff Oglethorpe University - Atlanta, GA 30319 Apply Overview Position Type Part-Time Staff Education Level High School Diploma Required Apply Description Job Description Summary: This position will assist the University Events and Information Technology Department in setting up, operating, and troubleshooting audiovisual (A/V) equipment for university-wide events, external events, and summer camps.  This role is critical in ensuring the smooth execution of events by providing on-site A/V support and collaborating with the University Events Department, IT Department, Technical Theater Department, and other stakeholders to meet event-specific needs. Key Responsibilities: Set up and configure audio-visual equipment like projectors, screens, microphones, speakers, cameras, and lighting systems according to event requirements Connect cables and ensure proper signal flow for flawless audio and video delivery. Provide on-site technical support to presenters and attendees during events, addressing any equipment-related concerns in real-time Test A/V equipment functionality before events and proactively troubleshoot any issues to minimize disruptions Collaborate with University Events and IT to understand AV needs, requirements, and expectations for each event Coordinate room setups and layouts based on event requirements Maintain, clean, and store AV equipment responsibly after events Perform preventive maintenance and basic repairs on equipment, reporting issues to the appropriate personnel Keep an updated inventory of all AV equipment, including status and condition reports Respond promptly to technical requests from event organizers and attendees Providing basic training on equipment operation to users when needed Support live streaming and/or hybrid events as required Assist with sound checks and film scouts as needed Qualifications Required Skills and Qualifications Technical Knowledge: Strong understanding of audio-visual equipment, including microphones, speakers, projectors, and cameras Problem-solving: Ability to troubleshoot technical issues quickly and efficiently under pressure Customer Service: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to interact effectively with diverse groups of students, faculty, staff, and external clients Physical Ability: Ability to lift and move heavy equipment as part of the setup process Flexibility: Availability to work flexible hours for a minimum of 20 hours a week, including evenings and weekends, based on event schedules Preferred Qualifications: Experience providing A/V support for events, conferences, or performances. Familiarity with A/V software and control systems like Crestron or similar platforms. Basic understanding of live streaming platforms and hybrid event setups (Microsoft Teams). Prior experience working in higher education or with large-scale event support. Additional Notes: This position requires a strong commitment to excellent service and a proactive approach to problem-solving. Training on specific equipment and systems the University uses will be provided. Ideal for individuals pursuing technology, event management, or media production careers. Share job details to About OGLETHORPE UNIVERSITY INC Oglethorpe University Turner Lynch Campus Center Stormy Petrel Academic Quad Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/E89EC0BE36E642B4CF9B1208D8AFD807/jobs/351119": {
      "title": "Admission Counselor",
      "description": "Admission Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Admission Counselor Oglethorpe University - Atlanta, GA 30319 Apply Overview Position Type Full-Time Staff Education Level Bachelor's Category Education Apply Description The Office of Admissions seeks an energetic, flexible, and detail-oriented person for the Admissions Counselor position. Reporting to the Senior Director of Admission, this person recruits prospective students and meets enrollment goals for one or more of Oglethorpe University’s degree programs through regional recruitment, on-campus and virtual programs, and serves as the Admissions athletic liaison and project work. Recruitment travel will be focused in metro Atlanta and out-of-state territories. Duties and Responsibilities: Manage all aspects of recruitment for an assigned geographic territory Develop a comprehensive prospect pool in your territory Use data from our CRM to strategically schedule and participate in high school visits and college fairs Maintain sustained communication with all prospective students and families, high school counselors Intentionally develop and maintain strategic relationships with high school counselors Ensure the accuracy of data in our CRM Assist with and attend all on-campus events Advise and consult with prospective students and families on admission to Oglethorpe Deliver contextually appropriate presentations and visit experiences Engage in intentional and continual learning about the offerings of an Oglethorpe education and best practices in the field of Admission Create a warm and inclusive atmosphere on campus Answer questions thoughtfully and thoroughly for families; provide exceptional customer service Review and evaluate applicants for admission Critically evaluate applicants for admission based on Oglethorpe’s institutional priorities and goals Follow up with students and families at all stages of the admission cycle to reach enrollment goals Review Athletic Customer Relationship Management System for Admissions alignment Serve as an ambassador of the Oglethorpe University brand at all times Other duties as assigned Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree and 1 year of work experience. Excellent communication (verbal, written, and digital) and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Ability to work in a fluid environment, prioritize goals and independently manage multiple, diverse, competing priorities while meeting deadlines. Strong problem-solving skills and ability to work independently and collaboratively Must successfully pass a criminal background check. Additional Information: This is a full-time, 12-month position with extensive travel. A valid driver’s license and personal automobile are required. Working evenings and some weekends required Position tasks are generally required to be performed in person.  Work-from-home options may be granted at the supervisors’ discretion. Oglethorpe reserves the right to change remote work status with notice to the employee. Some heavy lifting may be required. Share job details to About OGLETHORPE UNIVERSITY INC Oglethorpe University Turner Lynch Campus Center Stormy Petrel Academic Quad Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
